{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Human Factors.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Human Factors.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"human factors human factors","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Human Factors.md","fileName":"Human Factors.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Human Factors","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[UX Evaluation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["UX Evaluation","3D User Interface","Perception","Cognition","Attention","Physical Ergonomics","User-Centered Design","Usability Engineering","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Human Factors.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Human Factors.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"human factors human factors","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Human Factors.md","fileName":"Human Factors.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Human Factors","heading":"Human Factors","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Human factors are the capabilities, characteristics, and limitations of the person using a system. They include the body acting, the senses perceiving, and the brain thinking.\n\nHuman-factors-driven design studies what people can comfortably and reliably do, then uses that knowledge to pursue safe, efficient, and effective interaction. In a [[3D User Interface]], relevant areas include [[Perception]], [[Cognition]], [[Attention]], and [[Physical Ergonomics]]. These factors are interconnected, so evaluation may need to isolate particular issues without forgetting their relationships.\n\nHuman factors form a foundation for [[User-Centered Design]] and [[Usability Engineering]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["UX Evaluation","3D User Interface","Perception","Cognition","Attention","Physical Ergonomics","User-Centered Design","Usability Enginee